.TH TUI_TEXTVIEW_INIT 3 2026-10-03 "libtuikit 0.1" "libtuikit Manual"
.SH NAME
tui_textview_init, tui_textview_free, tui_textview_set_text,
tui_textview_append, tui_textview_wrap, tui_textview_lines,
tui_textview_scroll, tui_textview_scroll_to, tui_textview_scroll_end,
tui_textview_at_end, tui_textview_top, tui_textview_handle,
tui_textview_render \- word-wrapped, scrollable text
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <tuikit/textview.h>
.PP
.BI "void tui_textview_init(tui_textview *" tv );
.BI "void tui_textview_free(tui_textview *" tv );
.BI "int  tui_textview_set_text(tui_textview *" tv ", const char *" text );
.BI "int  tui_textview_append(tui_textview *" tv ", const char *" text ", size_t " n );
.BI "int  tui_textview_wrap(tui_textview *" tv ", int " cols );
.BI "int  tui_textview_lines(const tui_textview *" tv );
.BI "void tui_textview_scroll(tui_textview *" tv ", int " delta );
.BI "void tui_textview_scroll_to(tui_textview *" tv ", int " line );
.BI "void tui_textview_scroll_end(tui_textview *" tv );
.BI "int  tui_textview_at_end(const tui_textview *" tv );
.BI "int  tui_textview_top(const tui_textview *" tv );
.BI "int  tui_textview_handle(tui_textview *" tv ", const tui_event *" ev );
.BI "void tui_textview_render(tui_textview *" tv ", tui_canvas " c ", tui_style " st );
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
A text view shows a text \(em a message, a mail body, an issue
description, a log \(em wrapped to the width it is drawn at, and scrolls
through it.
It keeps its own copy of the text.
.PP
.BR tui_textview_set_text ()
replaces the text and scrolls to the top.
.BR tui_textview_append ()
adds to it: a view that showed the end (or showed nothing yet) follows
what is appended, and a view the user scrolled elsewhere stays where it
is \(em a chat history or a streamed answer does not move under a reader.
.PP
.BR tui_textview_render ()
wraps the text to the canvas width if it changed, clears the canvas with
.IR st ,
and draws the visible lines.
Lines break at spaces and tabs where they can, inside a word where they
must; the spaces at a break are not drawn; a wide character is never
split; a tab advances to the next multiple of eight columns.
A CR before LF is dropped and a text ending in a newline has no empty last
line; other control characters are drawn as U+00B7.
When the width changes, the line at the top stays at the top, and a view
showing the end keeps showing the end.
.PP
.BR tui_textview_wrap ()
wraps explicitly, e.g. to learn the line count before drawing.
The scroll functions keep the view within the text: the last line can
come to the bottom of the view, not above it.
.BR tui_textview_handle ()
applies Up, Down, PgUp, PgDn (one view less one line), Home and End, and
the shared letters for them
.RB ( j ", " k ", " ctrl\-f ", " ctrl\-b ", " g ", " G ,
as in
.BR tui_listview_handle (3)),
and returns 1 for them, 0 for other events.
.SH RETURN VALUE
.BR tui_textview_set_text (),
.BR tui_textview_append ()
return 0, or \-1 with
.I errno
.RB ( EINVAL ,
.BR ENOMEM ;
the old text stays).
.BR tui_textview_wrap ()
returns the number of lines or \-1.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tui_listview_init (3),
.BR tui_canvas_of (3),
.BR libtuikit (7)
